[b]Single player only. Build 42.[/b]

Pick the vehicle that's parked near you when a new game starts, right on the character creation screen. Any installed vehicle (KI5, vanilla or other mods), with its paint, parts and cargo, and a trailer or camper behind it.

[h2]How to use[/h2]
[list]
[*]Click Starting Vehicle, next to Random. The window looks like the mechanics screen, with a 3D view you can turn and zoom.
[*]Click a part to choose it. KI5 add-ons (bullbars, snorkels, window armor, roof racks) take any item that fits, or None. Tires, brakes, suspension and the like offer their grades. Game's choice lets the game roll it.
[*]Select the trunk or glove box to pack it.
[*]Trailer tab: a trailer or camper with its own paint, parts and cargo.
[*]Save builds by name and load them later.
[/list]

[h2]Options[/h2]
Sandbox page "Starting Vehicle":
[list]
[*]Spawn the chosen vehicle: on
[*]Part condition, fuel, battery charge: 100%
[*]Key in your pocket (off puts it in the glove box): on
[*]Parking search radius: 30 tiles
[*]Allow a trailer, Allow cargo: on
[/list]

[h2]Compatibility[/h2]
[list]
[*]KI5 vehicles need no setup, and KI5's library won't re-roll your add-on picks.
[*]If a spawn-location mod such as Spawn Selector moves you far away, the vehicle is parked again near the new spot (until you get in, 3 moves or 10 minutes).
[*]Single player only. In multiplayer nothing spawns.
[/list]

[h2]Known issues[/h2]
[list]
[*]Vanilla cars list paints as Paint 1, Paint 2 and so on, and their 3D view shows every part model.
[*]A few KI5 tires and bumpers show a sibling's model in the 3D view. The spawned vehicle is right.
[*]If the hitches don't line up, the trailer is left behind the car unhitched.
[/list]

Source and bug reports: [url=https://github.com/maxcwolf/pz-mods/tree/main/choose-starting-vehicle]GitHub[/url]
